# Cloudflare Pages redirects (QUESTIONS Q21, R15). Docs:
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/
#
# The site is a Next.js static export with trailingSlash: false: /exams is served
# from exams.html. These rules make the clean URL the only one. No destination ends in
# ".html" or "/" (except the root, which no source can produce again), so no rule can match
# its own output and nothing loops. Pages then serves the clean URL from the .html file
# without any redirect of its own. First match wins.
#
# www -> apex is a domain-level redirect, which _redirects cannot express: it is a
# Cloudflare Redirect Rule / Bulk Redirect (LAUNCH_CHECKLIST.md).

# .html -> clean URL (Pages would answer these with its own 308; one explicit 301 hop).
/index.html  /  301
/hi/index.html  /hi  301
/*.html  /:splat  301

# Trailing slash -> no slash. The root "/" does not match (the pattern needs two slashes).
/*/  /:splat  301
